WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.820
Jim, wait.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:11.950
I want you to take this.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:14.160
The key to your chest?

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:19.350
Yes, inside you'll find a document wrapped in oil paper.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.830
I beg you...
Don't let them take it.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.290
I'm counting on you, Jim.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:27.790
<i>Captain Billy is dead.</i>

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.720
<i>And thus, my mother and I
have opened his chest.</i>

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:37.140
That's it!

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.890
No mistake, this is it!

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.780
<i>Then they came.</i>

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.160
Mother, hurry!

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.900
Hurry!

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.020
M-Mother!

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.510
You alright, mother?

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.510
I'll be fine, I just twisted my ankle.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:12.420
Lean on me.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.970
Treasure
Island

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.770
Takarajima

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.580
saa ikou

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.580
Come, let's go

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.670
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.670
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.510
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.510
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.390
umi hedeyou

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.390
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.310
ikute ni wa

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.310
Many of us

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.310
minna mada shiranai

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.310
Still don't know of

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.060
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.060
The days and nights full of mystery

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.560
matte iru darou

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.560
That await us there

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.070
itsumo shinji you

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.070
We must always have trust

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.320
magokoro wo

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.320
And be sincere

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:19.580
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:19.580
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.710
tade hitotsu no

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.710
I only...

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.130
akogare dake wa

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.130
...have one desire

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.420
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.420
And no one...

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:35.130
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:35.130
...will ever take it away

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.090
tade hitotsu no

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.090
I only...

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.390
akogare dake wa

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.390
...have one desire

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.720
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.720
And no one...

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:53.650
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:53.650
...will ever take it away

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:04.540
episode

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:04.540
I've got the map
to Treasure Island!

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.090
Come on, mom, hurry!

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.480
M-Mother!

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.560
Hold on, mom.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.690
That's it, guys!
We're almost there!

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:58.500
Don't let Billy take it first!

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.900
Don't forget that he isn't our captain anymore!

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.470
Show no mercy!

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:08.670
We must retrieve that document at all costs, scurvy dogs!

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.590
B-Billy...!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.440
H-He's dead...!

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.400
Billy is dead.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.610
Wh-What did you say?
He's dead?

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.940
It's true, for him to be on
his way to the other world...

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.850
...must be because he was expecting us.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:54.460
What are you waiting for?!
Search him, hurry up!

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.650
Find me that document!

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:58.730
We heard you.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.770
No need to shout.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:11.580
Sorry, Pew, but he has nothing on him.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:12.920
Nothing?

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:16.790
Then it must be in his room!
Go upstairs and search his room!

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.540
Come on, guys, upstairs!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.920
Yeah, let's go!

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:36.850
Is there someone there?

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:42.780
Hey!

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.030
B-Bad news, old man Pew!

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:49.990
Billy's chest has been searched thoroughly!

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.450
Wh-What?

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.210
Damn it all...

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:07.430
Come on, mom.
Here's our chance to slip away!

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:08.090
Okay...

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.290
You holding on, mom?

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.140
Yes, I'm fine.

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.200
And your ankle?

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:39.160
It's fine, it's nothing.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.940
And you?
You holding on?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.210
As you can see, I feel great!

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:45.590
Benbow?

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.590
Where are you, Benbow?

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.890
<i>He couldn't be...!</i>

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:03.730
Nothing?

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.070
Nothing at all?

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:07.990
No trace of Flint's document?!

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.550
But you know, old man Pew,
we didn't come for nothing.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:23.670
Like I'm interested in some change.
All that matters is Flint's document!

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:27.280
But we've searched everywhere.
It aint here!

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.990
Someone got here before us...

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:35.040
Curses.
Who could have done this?

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.540
Who dared to double-cross us?

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.120
In any case, our thief...

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:44.980
...had to know that Billy
possessed that document.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.720
I-It's the kid!
It's the kid!

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.610
It must be him!

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.200
Find me that little brat!

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:56.120
Got it?!
Do what you must to find him!

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.540
Wh-What's that sound?

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.750
Hurry! Downstairs!

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.290
Wh-What is that?!

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.100
Take that!

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.230
Look, it's just a cat.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:25.150
Get to work, you swabs!
Search the inn!

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:30.320
Search every corner!
He could still be hiding here!

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.370
Come on out!

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.760
You bastard...!

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:10.430
Damn it, what a bunch of vandals!

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:16.160
Mother and I worked so hard to run our treasured Admiral Benbow inn and yet...

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.450
Damn pirates!

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:19.080
Gotcha!

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:27.540
Stupid blowfish! Search for the document instead of the cat!

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:28.840
Benbow!

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:41.560
Benbow!

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.890
Over here.
Come here, boy...

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.950
There you are, eh, lad.

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:21.550
Hey, old man Pew found the kid!

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.730
Now, where is the document, lad?

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.610
Where is Flint's document?

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:40.700
I-I don't know what you're talking about!

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:44.120
I'm talking about the paper you stole from Billy.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:47.160
Come, come, don't take me for an idiot.

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:50.120
I-I didn't steal it!

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.460
You didn't steal it?

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:58.090
So you admit that you're the one who has it.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:02.430
Time to hand it over.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:03.920
Come on, give me the parchm—

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:05.140
You won't have it!

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.180
I promised the captain—Billy Bones!

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:08.800
Damn you!

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.100
Get off, damn brat!

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:13.560
G-Get back!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.480
D-Don't come any closer or I'll shoot!

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:30.380
Curses.
This dirty little brat has a pistol.

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:34.370
What are you waiting for?
Hurry up and catch him!

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.560
Know when to give up, dirty brat!

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:48.480
You little...!

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:55.900
J-Jim!

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:02.420
You've played enough with that pistol, laddie!

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:05.960
Hand it over!
Give us Flint's document!

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:09.400
Never!
I'd rather die than give it to you!

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:11.100
Now you've said it!

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:18.050
Stay there, kid!

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:22.640
Catch this!

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:28.390
He's climbing the stairs!
Block the way!

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:44.860
You idiots! You can't even catch a kid?!
Hurry up and grab him!

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:46.040
Take that!

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:08.550
Get down here!

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:12.520
Hey! Let me go! Let me go!
Damn you, I said let go!

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:15.810
You've given us a hard time, dirty little monkey.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:20.450
Thank you, Benbow!

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:22.610
Hey, kid!

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.260
This little game is over!

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.780
Now, give us back Flint's document!

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:30.540
If you don't, you can say goodbye to your dear mother!

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.200
Damn it!
How dare you threaten Mother—

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.200
Come on, hurry up and give us the paper.

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:39.960
Patience isn't our virtue.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:41.940
Wretches!

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:45.510
Bunch of cowards!
And you call yourselves sailors?!

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:49.340
You can say that if you want, it doesn't bother me.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:52.620
I'm going to count to three and at three...

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.380
Jim, don't listen!

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:57.350
Here I go.
One...

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:00.120
Two...

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:01.260
And... three.

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:02.130
And... three.

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:07.780
It's the signal!

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:12.420
Hey guys, we have to get away.

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:14.270
Bunch of cowards!

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:18.420
Even so, old man Pew, two whistles mean that it's serious and we have to get away!

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:23.220
Idiot. We have to get our hands on the document first!

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:28.060
With it, you'll be rich!
As rich as kings!

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:32.350
Or do you want to continue
living like less than nothing,

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:35.820
begging for a bottle of rum, you swabs?

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:37.270
Well, not me!

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.070
Th-They're coming in droves!

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.400
It's the police force!

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:51.990
Everyone run!

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.550
Shit, run for your lives!

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:02.750
Mother!
Are you alright?

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:04.480
I'm alright.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:06.440
Hey, hey, hey!
Wait for me, mateys!

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:09.180
You cannot leave old Pew!

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:10.720
Not good ol' Pew!

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.850
And you call yourself pirates?!

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:15.770
We sailed the seven seas together!

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:19.250
M-Mates, where did you run off to?!

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:25.190
You're nothing but a bunch of cowards!

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.280
<i>Damn it! What an idiot...</i>

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.910
<i>Yes, what an idiot I've been...</i>

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.180
Th-This person...

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.900
It's a pirate.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:00.860
He was called Blind Pew.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.300
D-Damn it all...

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:03.770
The treasure...

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:05.810
The treasure.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.150
The treasure?

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.400
Where is it?

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:11.400
Where is it?
Where is Flint's—the old man's...

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.830
...par...ch...ment.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:18.240
Flint's document?

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:25.060
The people from the village warned us,

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:26.890
but this is truly terrible.

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.680
Don't worry, mom.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:38.310
You can count on me.
I will fix up the Benbow Inn.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:42.880
What are you saying? I will help you every step of the way.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:46.060
Well, the important thing is that you're safe.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.440
It's thanks to my son.

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:52.030
Jim, you're really your father's son.

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:55.170
But of course I am!

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.760
Th-That's right...

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:14.370
Wait!

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:16.970
Please wait a second!

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:26.540
Captain, here are the seashells that you kept.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:29.950
And, although it's broken, your spyglass.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.730
<i>One more thing, Captain...</i>

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:36.390
<i>Like I promised, I won't give them Flint's document.</i>

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:43.700
Fifteen men...

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:47.810
...on a dead man's chest!

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:54.140
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:58.100
Drink and the devil...

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:03.060
...had done for the rest!

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:13.160
Goodbye, Captain.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:16.420
Jim... Jim!

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:17.450
Y-Yes?

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:21.940
Can you come with us to see {Squire}Mr. Trelawney?

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:23.660
To see {Squire}Mr. Trelawney?

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:27.740
Dr. Livesey spent the day hunting with Mr. Trelawney.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:30.460
Now Trelawney has returned to the mansion.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.700
I'd rather it be you...

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:36.220
...who tells them what happened at the inn tonight.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:37.420
Yes, I understand.

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:41.620
Come, hang on tight!

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:42.140
Okay.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.820
Okay, I'm going to start cleaning up.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.940
Jim will be very surprised when he returns.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:05.650
A treasure, Flint and a document...

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:08.330
Good work.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.190
If I my, I will retire.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:15.300
L-Livesey!

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:19.260
Just from listening to this story my heart is beating wildly.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.930
I can't stay still, you see?

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:25.020
Don't you feel the same?
Flint is not just anyone.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:29.330
That well-known pirate has scoured the seven seas of the world.

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:33.980
What's more, some say the treasures he has amassed...

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:39.650
...are worth as much as the King of England's riches.

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.430
If it just so happens to be...

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:45.710
...that the document precisely points the way to the location of the famous treasure...

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:48.700
...then the pirates would kill each other to get it.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:52.140
It is exactly as you say!
You see where I'm coming from?

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:54.300
Yes, it's very possible.

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:58.000
Still, there has to be a reason
why this document exists.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.130
Y-Yes, I guess so...

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.780
It's nothing but a dream, Trelawney.

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:05.060
Pirate's treasure, Flint's gold...

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:07.340
It's every man's dream.

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:09.640
People have such imagination.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:11.150
That it is.

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:12.770
It isn't a dream!

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:18.850
It isn't a dream. It exists.
Such a document exists!

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:20.490
Look, here it is.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:23.280
The Captain didn't want the pirates to find it.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:38.670
It's a map!

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:48.850
Look!

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.810
"Bulk of Treasure Sump"...

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:53.640
A treasure map!

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.770
It's the treasure map!
It must be Flint's map!

00:20:57.180 --> 00:21:00.440
It's the map to Treasure Island!
The map to Treasure Island, I say!

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.400
The map to Treasure Island...

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:04.530
Treasure Island...

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:06.360
Treasure Island!

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:08.740
Livesey, I'm going.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:12.860
Quit your ridiculous profession immediately.

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:18.180
It's decided. Tomorrow I'm off to Bristol
to buy the most beautiful boat in England.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:21.210
Then, I'm headed for Treasure Island!

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:27.340
We will have bread on board, Livesey.

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:29.160
But, Trelawney...

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:31.140
It's the dream of every man!

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:34.100
The dream of every man...
Yeah, I'm coming with you!

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:38.460
This is no child's errand.
That's not going to happen.

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:42.100
Now, Livesey, follow me
and we'll discuss all of this.

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:44.070
W-Wait a minute, Mr. Trelawney!

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:47.720
What? Oh, very well.
Since it's late, you can sleep here.

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:50.450
Go ahead, you can take one of the rooms on the first floor.

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:57.540
What the hell, Mr. Trelawney.

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:59.810
He's out of his mind.

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:02.800
Even when I'm the one who brought the document.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:04.700
<i>Treasure Island...</i>

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:06.460
<i>It's decided, I will go with them!</i>

00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:08.300
<i>I'm definitely going with them!</i>

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:10.760
<i>Yes...
Oh, yeah!</i>

00:22:27.940 --> 00:22:31.750
To      be        continued

00:22:32.670 --> 00:22:37.710
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:32.670 --> 00:22:37.710
Hey sea breeze

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:43.520
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:43.520
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:49.730
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:49.730
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:49.730 --> 00:22:55.170
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:49.730 --> 00:22:55.170
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.170 --> 00:23:00.580
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.170 --> 00:23:00.580
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:00.580 --> 00:23:06.040
kaban ippai no

00:23:00.580 --> 00:23:06.040
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:11.670
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:11.670
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:17.530
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:17.530
Will be brought back

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:24.120
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:24.120
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:30.010
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:30.010
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:39.730
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:39.730
I blow out a whistle

00:23:44.540 --> 00:23:46.240
I'm the one who found the map.

00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:49.400
Having it taken from me because they think I'm a child is unfair!

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:51.450
I wanna go! I wanna go! I wanna go!

00:23:52.080 --> 00:23:56.120
But... Dr. Livesey has presented an issue.

00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:58.240
Do I have the right to leave my mother all alone?

00:23:58.790 --> 00:24:03.240
The next day, mother makes me a real feast.

00:24:03.240 --> 00:24:05.040
Why is mother doing this?

